From e971d6f45417fb15782b63f60f726c12e339f1c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhilash Koka <abhilash.koka1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 20:26:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add character lock and costume lock/change to the Video
 Studio
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Reference-anchored character consistency: a tenant creates a character
(described → AI-generated full-body reference, or an uploaded photo) and
every costume is an identity-preserving gpt-image-1 edit of that same
reference. Video engines then anchor generation to the locked outfit's
image, so the same character — in the same costume, unless the wardrobe
plan changes it — appears across scenes and videos.

Two surfaces:
- Text to Video: pick a character (+ outfit) and the clip becomes
  keyframe-edit → image-to-video instead of raw text-to-video.
- Topic to Video: a new 'Your character' visuals mode replaces stock
  footage with AI scenes. Narration cues are partitioned into balanced
  scenes (4 per paragraph); one LLM call plans each scene's visual and
  outfit, honoring the locked default and the user's wardrobe notes
  (costume changes at story moments); scenes generate concurrently
  (keyframe + i2v, one retry) and compose through the existing
  narration/subtitle/music pipeline via an explicit scene map.

Billing: character story videos reserve one video unit per scene
(Short 4 / Medium 8 / Long 12), all-or-nothing, refunded on failure;
usage meters one row per unit so quota accounting matches. Character
reference and outfit generations fund exactly like image generations.

CRUD: /characters endpoints (list/create/delete, outfit add/remove,
default outfit protected), tenant-scoped, gated by the videoGen kill
switch, with a Characters manager dialog + pickers in the studio.

Verified: full typecheck clean; api-server 1072/1072 (26 new), web
306/306 (2 new), mobile 149/149; spec lint + codegen drift clean;
db push applies the two new tables cleanly.

